Priority: 2
Area: Canvas
Status: done
Depends on: fix-select-tool, add-element-resize

Goal:
Bring freehand strokes into the editable selection workflow instead of leaving them as second-class items after selection.

Context:
Strokes can already be hit-tested, but the recent resize work intentionally excluded them. The user explicitly wants strokes to participate in selection behavior more fully.

Expected changes:

- improve selected-state affordances for strokes
- define first-pass stroke editing behavior within the selection model
- make sure later batch-style edits can include strokes

Acceptance criteria:

- A selected stroke has clear visible feedback and remains stable under normal selection interactions.
- Stroke selections participate correctly in later multi-select and style-edit flows.
- Any intentional limits on stroke resize/edit behavior are explicit and documented.

Notes:

- This task does not have to invent full geometric stroke-resize semantics if a narrower first pass is more reliable.
